        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 10,
        "titulo": "The superlative, step by step",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: to say \"the most …\", there are TWO forms. FORM 1: «am» + adjective + «-sten», after a verb like sein: «Der Zug ist am schnellsten» (the train is the fastest). FORM 2: «der/die/das» + adjective + «-ste» + noun, when the noun follows (with the adjective ending!): «der schnellste Zug» (the fastest train), «die schönste Stadt», «das beste Essen». STEP 2: adjectives ending in -d, -t, -s, -ß, -z, -sch take «-esten»: am ältesten, am heißesten. STEP 3: the umlaut comes along: am ältesten, am größten, am stärksten. STEP 4: irregular forms: gut → am besten (best); viel → am meisten (most); gern → am liebsten (most of all, favorite); hoch → am höchsten; nah → am nächsten. STEP 5: a typical sentence: «Im Sommer ist es am wärmsten» (it's warmest in summer). STEP 6: show the group with «von» or the genitive: «der schönste von allen» (the most beautiful of all).",
